{
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 0.8,
 "tail": 2.0,
 "footer": "Sources: canada.ca \u00b7 CRA T4037 Capital gains; line 12700 and Schedule 3; capital losses; Finance Canada / CRA updates on the cancelled inclusion-rate increase \u00b7 Examples, general info, not advice",
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "L1",
   "file": "vo/L1.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Leah sold her shares and made eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety dollars of profit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2",
   "file": "vo/L2.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Her income tax on that profit: about one thousand, nine hundred and twenty-eight dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3",
   "file": "vo/L3.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If the same eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety dollars had been fully taxed, like salary or interest, the income tax would be about three thousand, seven hundred and five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L4",
   "file": "vo/L4.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same money. About half the tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "L5",
   "file": "vo/L5.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And one simple move cut her bill by another five hundred and ninety-three dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L6",
   "file": "vo/L6.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "By the end of this video, you'll know exactly how a capital gain is taxed in Canada, step by step, with real numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "L7",
   "file": "vo/L7.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "All numbers: twenty twenty-six, Ontario, a seventy thousand dollar salary. Examples, not real people. General information, not advice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L8",
   "file": "vo/L8.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "First: what a capital gain actually is."
  },
  {
   "id": "L9",
   "file": "vo/L9.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "A capital gain is the profit when you sell something for more than it cost you. Shares, funds, a cottage, a rental property."
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "vo/L10.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The key word is sell. If your shares go up but you keep them, there's nothing to report yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "vo/L11.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For most people, that means shares or funds held in a regular investment account, outside an R R S P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "vo/L12.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The gain is taxed in the year you sell. Not the year you bought, and not while the price goes up and down."
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "vo/L13.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And if you sell for less than it cost you, that's a capital loss. We'll come back to that, because it matters."
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "vo/L14.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, Leah's numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "vo/L15.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Leah earns seventy thousand dollars a year in Ontario."
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "vo/L16.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "A few years ago, she bought four hundred shares at fifty dollars each. Twenty thousand dollars. Plus a ten dollar commission."
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "vo/L17.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That commission counts. Her cost isn't twenty thousand. It's twenty thousand and ten dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "vo/L18.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The C R A calls this your adjusted cost base. It's what you paid, plus the costs of buying."
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "vo/L19.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "This year, she sells all four hundred shares at eighty dollars each. Thirty-two thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "vo/L20.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Thirty-two thousand, minus twenty thousand and ten. Her capital gain is eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "vo/L21.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now comes the part that makes capital gains different."
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "vo/L22.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Only half of a capital gain is taxable."
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "vo/L23.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The government calls this the inclusion rate. For twenty twenty-six, it's one half."
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "vo/L24.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "You may remember a plan to raise it to two thirds. That increase was cancelled in March twenty twenty-five. The rate stayed at one half."
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "vo/L25.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So of Leah's eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety dollars, only five thousand, nine hundred and ninety-five dollars is added to her income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "vo/L26.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The other half isn't taxed at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "vo/L27.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "She reports the sale on Schedule three of her return, and the taxable half goes on line one two seven hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "vo/L28.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "From there, it's taxed like any other income, at her own federal and Ontario rates."
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "vo/L29.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "In other words, a capital gain is taxed at about half of your usual rate on extra income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "vo/L30.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So let's see the real bill."
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "vo/L31.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Five thousand, nine hundred and ninety-five dollars of extra taxable income, on top of a seventy thousand dollar salary."
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "vo/L32.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Her income tax goes up by about one thousand, nine hundred and twenty-eight dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "vo/L33.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "That's about sixteen percent of her total profit. She keeps about ten thousand and sixty-two dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "vo/L34.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Now compare. If the same eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety dollars were fully taxed, the income tax would be about three thousand, seven hundred and five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "vo/L35.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "She'd keep about eight thousand, two hundred and eighty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "vo/L36.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same amount of money. One thousand, seven hundred and seventy-seven dollars less tax, just because it's a capital gain."
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "vo/L37.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "At seventy thousand dollars, Leah's rate on extra income is about thirty-one percent. On a capital gain, it works out to about sixteen."
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "vo/L38.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And one more thing: her employer's payroll knows nothing about this sale. So the tax on it usually shows up when she files her return, not on her paycheque."
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "vo/L39.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "But here's what most people miss."
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "vo/L40.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "There's no single capital gains tax rate. The half that's taxable lands on top of everything else you earned that year."
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "vo/L41.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So the same gain costs different people different amounts."
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "vo/L42.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If Leah's income that year were forty thousand dollars, the tax on the same gain would be about one thousand, one hundred and forty-two."
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "vo/L43.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "At one hundred and twenty thousand dollars, about two thousand, six hundred and two."
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "vo/L44.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Same shares. Same profit. The bill more than doubles, depending on the rest of her income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "vo/L45.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And because the gain is taxed in the year you sell, the year you choose can matter."
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "vo/L46.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "A year with lower income, like a year back at school, on leave, or in early retirement, means a lower rate on the taxable half."
  },
  {
   "id": "L47",
   "file": "vo/L47.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the move that saved Leah another five hundred and ninety-three dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L48",
   "file": "vo/L48.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Remember capital losses?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L49",
   "file": "vo/L49.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The same year, Leah also owned a stock that had dropped. She'd paid more for it than it was worth now. On paper, a four thousand dollar loss."
  },
  {
   "id": "L50",
   "file": "vo/L50.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "She sold it too. Now the loss is real, and it's reported in the same year as her gain."
  },
  {
   "id": "L51",
   "file": "vo/L51.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One warning: if you sell at a loss and buy the same shares right back, the loss can be denied. The C R A calls that a superficial loss, so check the rules first."
  },
  {
   "id": "L52",
   "file": "vo/L52.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Capital losses reduce capital gains. Eleven thousand, nine hundred and ninety, minus four thousand. Her net gain is seven thousand, nine hundred and ninety."
  },
  {
   "id": "L53",
   "file": "vo/L53.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Only half of that is taxable. Her tax drops to about one thousand, three hundred and thirty-five dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L54",
   "file": "vo/L54.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Five hundred and ninety-three dollars less, because she reported a loss she'd already had."
  },
  {
   "id": "L55",
   "file": "vo/L55.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One rule: capital losses only reduce capital gains. They can't reduce your salary."
  },
  {
   "id": "L56",
   "file": "vo/L56.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And losses you can't use this year don't disappear. They can be applied against capital gains in other years."
  },
  {
   "id": "L57",
   "file": "vo/L57.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's your capital gains checklist."
  },
  {
   "id": "L58",
   "file": "vo/L58.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Keep your purchase records, including commissions. That's your adjusted cost base."
  },
  {
   "id": "L59",
   "file": "vo/L59.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Report every sale on Schedule three, gains and losses."
  },
  {
   "id": "L60",
   "file": "vo/L60.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Remember that only half of the gain is taxed, at your own rate."
  },
  {
   "id": "L61",
   "file": "vo/L61.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Before you sell, think about which year the gain will land in, and whether you have losses to use."
  },
  {
   "id": "L62",
   "file": "vo/L62.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And one exception to know about: selling the home you live in is usually different. That's the principal residence exemption, and we covered it in an earlier video."
  },
  {
   "id": "L63",
   "file": "vo/L63.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So, what did we learn?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L64",
   "file": "vo/L64.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. A capital gain is taxed only when you sell."
  },
  {
   "id": "L65",
   "file": "vo/L65.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Only half of it is taxable in twenty twenty-six."
  },
  {
   "id": "L66",
   "file": "vo/L66.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. There's no flat rate. Your other income decides what the gain really costs."
  },
  {
   "id": "L67",
   "file": "vo/L67.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Losses reduce gains, this year or in other years."
  },
  {
   "id": "L68",
   "file": "vo/L68.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Next on this channel: why a one hundred thousand dollar salary does not mean one hundred thousand dollars of taxable income. Subscribe, so you don't miss it."
  }
 ],
